# Authorship Header

When **creating any new file**, add an author and creation-date header to the
file's module docstring (or the language's idiomatic top-of-file comment).

- **Author:** `Pandiyaraj Karuppasamy`
- **Date:** the file's creation date, formatted `<Mon-DD-YYYY>` (three-letter
  month, e.g. `Jul-18-2026`).

## Python

```python
"""
Short one-line description of the module.

Author: Pandiyaraj Karuppasamy
Date: Jul-18-2026
"""
```

If the file already has a multi-line docstring, append `Author:` / `Date:` just
before the closing `"""`. Expand a single-line docstring into the multi-line
form.

## Other languages

Use the idiomatic top-of-file comment, keeping the same two fields and format:

```csharp
// Short description.
//
// Author: Pandiyaraj Karuppasamy
// Date: Jul-18-2026
```

## Editing an existing file

Add or update a `Modified:` line directly after `Date:`:

```python
"""
Short one-line description of the module.

Author: Pandiyaraj Karuppasamy
Date: Jul-18-2026
Modified: Aug-02-2026
"""
```

- The `Date:` (creation) line **must never change**.
- If `Modified:` exists, set it to today's date; if absent, add it after `Date:`.
